  "slug": "dark-energy-543b",
  "summary": "DESI-era data are driving model comparisons and reconstructions that favor dynamical dark energy, with phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is testing whether dark energy departs from a cosmological constant using DESI BAO combined with CMB, supernova and lensing data. Model-specific comparisons within VCDM report that F42 is favored by AIC when supernovae are included. The Fading Dark Sector model is analyzed with DESI DR1 full-shape power spectra and outperforms CPL w0-wa. Two non-parametric reconstructions of dark-energy density and gravitational response find a phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7. Peripheral items address related probes: persistent-homology of 21-cm maps at Cosmic Dawn, a time-delay H0 trend whose significance falls to ~1σ with MST uncertainties, and a proposed universal ratio linking acceleration onset to the fσ8 turnover in flat ΛCDM as a consistency test.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
